CO2Fix_3_1

100	# simulation lenght [yr]

comments
{
Coffee-agroforestry plantation in the tropics (data from Costa Rica)
The Biomass Model has three cohorts:
  1) Canopy layer (shade tree): Cordia alliodora (100 trees per ha)
      - rotation 20 years,  MAI 7 m3/ha/yr over 20 yr. rotation period
  2) Intermediate layer (service tree): Erythrina poeppigiana
      - leaves and branches pruned annually and left to decompose; rotation 10 yrs.
  3) Understory: Coffea sp., renewed every 20 years
The wood from canopy layer trees is used for furniture

The CASFOR Case Study No.4 by Markku Kanninen, CATIE

Data principally from: 
Fassbender, H.W. 1993. Modelos edafológicos de sistemas agroforestales.
CATIE, Serie de Materiales de Enseñanza No. 29. 471 p.
}

